        <parameter>
            <valueName>layer:SOREM:1.0:Broadcast_Text</valueName>
            <value>At 9:25 p.m. Central Standard Time Saturday, Environment Canada has issued a tornado warning for South Central Saskatchewan. Extra care and attention should be exercised in and around the following localities: Prince Albert, Wahpeton Reserve, Meath Park, Davis and One Arrow Reserve. Environment Canada meteorologists are tracking a severe thunderstorm that is possibly producing a tornado. Damaging winds, large hail and locally intense rainfall are also possible. Take cover immediately if threatening weather approaches. Please consult local media for more information.</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>layer:EC-MSC-SMC:1.1:Designation_Code</valueName>
            <value>SK_00_01_LAND</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>layer:SOREM:2.0:WirelessImmediate</valueName>
            <value>Yes</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>layer:SOREM:2.0:WirelessText</valueName>
            <value>Environment Canada: TORNADO in this mobile coverage area.
Take immediate cover in a basement or interior room if weather threat approaches. Shelter from flying debris if outside.
Tornado Warning, 9:25 p.m. CST Saturday 11 July
</value>
